text:
Even though it's sad to see the Souls series go, they went out with a bang.
The last installment in the Dark Souls trilogy has, for me, most of the series greatest moments.
What they did right:
- Combat and gameplay is at it's best here;
- Level design for the most part is spot-on;
- The most amazing boss fights you will see in a videogame today, chills guaranteed;
- Amazing secrets, EVEN better than Ash Lake/Great Hollow from Dark Souls 1!;
- Absolutely top-notch DLC with some of the best and hardest bosses in all the series;
- Character questlines are not tedious anymore, don't require you to have them summoned to every boss to make their story progress;
- Some fan service that is always a good thing since it doesn't hurt the game's cohesion and pace;
- Awesome atmosphere as always;
Some tough love on what they got wrong:
- The lore and story lost a bit of steam in this one, but only because it seems like they're repeating everything said in the first two games but with different words. They went out of their way to bring back stuff thought forgotten in Dark Souls 2 and made it sound like Dark Souls 2 never happened resulting in the games' continuity being a cluster♥♥♥♥.
- They re-did the HUD that was perfected in Dark Souls 2 and turned it into a mix of the Bloodborne menu and a piece of♥♥♥♥♥♥ It literally is♥♥♥♥♥♥ The dissapearing HUD was awesome in Dark Souls 2, but in 3 they made it actually annoying since it doesn't popup when there's actually♥♥♥♥♥♥going on;
- They ♥♥♥♥ed up the multiplayer that 2 got so right. I haven't played the matches on the recently added arenas but the rest is plagued with♥♥♥♥♥♥decisions like making it impossible to invade anything other than a gank squad. The covenants are lame in this one. Sure, they have better lore, but they aren't as impactful in the multiplayer side of things;
- Graphics were actually a bit better in some areas of Dark Souls 2;
TL;DR:
You should play it. Even if you think you won't like it, give it a chance.
This game will give you an experience you will never forget.
If you are a newcomer to the series or a souls veteran, its still worth it (The same thing is true for Dark Souls 1)

Performance:
{Game can be run on a potato very well, I have a HP Envy M6 laptop with a 3rd gen i5 2.50Ghz 2 cores 4 logical, 8GB ram and a HD 4000 with 640GB of HDD space. I get 68-80 FPS on very low and low FOV.}
My view of the game so far:
{There is NO P2W what so ever. The cheaters are still an issue mainly the ones with private cheats that are still around and they are mainly in Battle Match mode and SOME in Demo 5v5-8v8 match modes. All guns are Perm when purchased with Gold in game currency. Random boxes are a hit and miss and not that great unless you dont mind putting money into the game to open the boxes many times. The Gold random box is hard to get drops and mainly drop Grenades and green smokes. New OHK guns are really nice. SMGs are very well too but some will argue that they need a nerf and such. Shotguns are eh right now. Snipers are done well and if they get hit in the head there is aim punch for them (Snipers only have Aim punch FYI.) }
Servers: {The servers are OKAY once they get more money I hope they upgrade to better servers I honestly also feel we seriously need that ping limit MANY North American players are VERY tired of going against the 190-300+ ping players and abusing those pings to have an advantage. MANY will argue about this but I feel that♥♥♥♥♥♥is a real ♥♥♥♥ing pain and needs to be delt with ASAP.}
Over all view:
{I highly suggest trying this game out for at least 2 hours and give it a chance, It can run on potatos, its easy to pick up, It works and feels like a few FPS games we ALL know about and compare it too. Hope my review helped, Enjoy the game!}
NEW UPDATE: They did NOT give NA a ping limit GG
Addition: Most of the casters for this game is NA, and EU are the one's who only got the ping limit test on their server all the others have no ping limits.
It's a fun game with friends nothing more. and I doubt it will hit ESL

